From: OpenMandriva
Subject: [PATCH] Bug 2054387 - Qt: reclaim activation after no-focus popup lifecycle

0017 kept Gecko chrome logically active when no-focus popups stole focus, but
on KDE/Wayland the compositor still restacks the parent behind other apps.
Thunderbird reproduces this after account setup when the app menu closes and
openPreferencesTab() runs: focus goes null after unmap and the window drops.

- raise()+requestActivate() (immediate + next event loop) when reclaiming
- NotePopupInteraction(): brief suppress window for popup show/hide and input
- On hide of no-focus popups/alerts, reclaim the transient parent
- Handle QEvent::WindowActivate/Deactivate separately from keyboard focus

--- a/widget/qt/nsWindow.h
+++ b/widget/qt/nsWindow.h
@@ -112,6 +112,16 @@
   // True when this window may become the active chrome window (not PiP/alert).
   bool ShouldAcceptActivate() const;
 
+  // Raise + requestActivate for chrome windows. Used when no-focus popups
+  // (app menus, doorhangers) would otherwise leave the parent demoted on
+  // KDE/Wayland after the popup maps or unmaps.
+  void ReclaimActivation();
+  // Same, deferred to the next event-loop turn (after Wayland map/unmap).
+  void ScheduleReclaimActivation();
+  // Suppress Gecko deactivation + reclaim for a short window (popup lifecycle).
+  void NotePopupInteraction();
+  bool ShouldSuppressDeactivation() const;
+
   void OnExpose();
   void OnResize(int aWidth, int aHeight);
   void OnMove(int aX, int aY);
